  {:id :no-print-dup-machinery,
   :title "print-dup / print-ctor are absent",
   :rationale
   "print-dup emits host-class-aware, read-eval-able\n                    forms keyed on Java types. mino prints EDN-readable\n                    forms through the ordinary printer; the print-dup\n                    dispatch and its print-ctor helper are not\n                    provided.",
   :since "v0.1.0",
   :affected [clojure.core/print-dup clojure.core/print-ctor],
   :category
   {:id :printer,
    :title "Printer behavior",
    :description
    "pr-str output for various values and dynamic-var states."}}
  {:id :no-host-name-munging,
   :title "Host symbol-name munging is absent",
   :rationale
   "munge and namespace-munge encode Clojure names\n                    into JVM-legal class and member names. mino emits\n                    no host symbols, so the munging step has no\n                    purpose.",
   :since "v0.1.0",
   :affected [clojure.core/munge clojure.core/namespace-munge],
   :category
   {:id :jvm-statics,
    :title "JVM-static value remap",
    :description
    "JVM-only statics remapped to dialect-native equivalents."}}
  {:id :no-read-eval,
   :title "*read-eval* is absent",
   :rationale
   "*read-eval* gates the JVM reader's #=() eval-on-read\n                    feature, which mino's reader does not provide; there\n                    is no host eval to guard, so the var is absent.",
   :since "v0.1.0",
   :affected [clojure.core/*read-eval*],
   :category
   {:id :jvm-statics,
    :title "JVM-static value remap",
    :description
    "JVM-only statics remapped to dialect-native equivalents."}}
  {:id :protocol-impl-internals,
   :title "Protocol-dispatch implementation internals are absent",
   :rationale
   "These are private-ish JVM dispatch internals: the\n                    protocol-fn cache, method-reset, impl/method lookup\n                    over host classes, and the iterator reduce helper.\n                    mino dispatches protocols through its own\n                    atom-keyed mechanism and does not expose the JVM\n                    internals.",
   :since "v0.1.0",
   :affected
   [clojure.core/-cache-protocol-fn
    clojure.core/-reset-methods
    clojure.core/find-protocol-impl
    clojure.core/find-protocol-method
    clojure.core.protocols/iterator-reduce!],
   :category
   {:id :type-system,
    :title "Type-system representation",
    :description
    "How type, class, and dispatch report a value's kind."}}
  {:id :no-reducers-forkjoin-pool,
   :title "reducers ForkJoin task/pool entry points are absent",
   :rationale
   "clojure.core.reducers/fjtask and /pool front a JVM\n                    ForkJoinPool for parallel fold. mino has no\n                    ForkJoin runtime, so fold runs sequentially and the\n                    pool entry points are absent.",
   :since "v0.1.0",
   :affected [clojure.core.reducers/fjtask clojure.core.reducers/pool],
   :category
   {:id :concurrency,
    :title "Concurrency primitives",
    :description "Atoms, refs, agents, futures, core.async behavior."}}
  {:id :no-instant-host-calendar,
   :title "read-instant-calendar / -timestamp are absent",
